  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\nAccording to the HTML specification, [suggestions for rendering the `sub` and `sup` elements](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/rendering.html#phrasing-content-3) include  `line-height: normal`.\n\n```css\nsub { vertical-align: sub; }\nsup { vertical-align: super; }\nsub, sup { line-height: normal; font-size: smaller; }\n```\n\nIt is not included in current major browsers, and there is a discrepancy between the specification and actual implementation.\n\nThis is likely due to leftover code from an older browser. For example, in Firefox, `line-height: normal` was removed in [Bug 1524897](https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1524897) in 2019.\n\n",
